WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.205
My name is Huckleberry Finn. If you’ve read a book called The Adventures of Tom Sawyer , you already know about

2
00:00:09.206 --> 00:00:12.031
me. But if you haven’t, it doesn’t

3
00:00:12.032 --> 00:00:21.244
matter. At the end of that book, my friend Tom and I found six thousand dollars, and each of us was allowed to keep

4
00:00:21.245 --> 00:00:32.947
half. Judge Thatcher invested the money for us, so Tom and I would never have to worry about not having enough money

5
00:00:32.948 --> 00:00:37.707
again. I didn’t have a home, so the Widow Douglas took me

6
00:00:37.708 --> 00:00:41.044
in. She said she was going to civilize

7
00:00:41.045 --> 00:00:47.923
me. She made me wear new clean clothes, and sit at the table to eat my

8
00:00:47.924 --> 00:00:54.088
meals. But I missed the way I used to live, wearing my old rags and fixing my own

9
00:00:54.089 --> 00:01:03.410
supper. The widow had a sister, Miss Watson, who was determined to teach me to spell. I couldn’t help wiggling

10
00:01:03.411 --> 00:01:09.775
around. "Huckleberry, sit up straight!" she scolded me. "Why can’t you try to

11
00:01:09.776 --> 00:01:14.132
behave?" All I could think about was how I wanted to get

12
00:01:14.133 --> 00:01:24.706
away. I needed a change, but I knew the widow and her sister would never understand, so I didn’t try to

13
00:01:24.707 --> 00:01:30.365
explain. By the time I went up to my room for bed, I felt sad and

14
00:01:30.366 --> 00:01:34.713
lonesome. I sat in a chair by the window and looked out at the

15
00:01:34.714 --> 00:01:38.632
night. I heard an owl hooting and a dog

16
00:01:38.633 --> 00:01:43.522
howling. It sounded to me as if they were mourning for someone who had

17
00:01:43.523 --> 00:01:47.851
died. It scared me, and I started to

18
00:01:47.852 --> 00:01:56.279
tremble. Then a spider crawled up on my shoulder, and when I shook it off, it fell into my candle and burned

19
00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:07.068
up. I knew that killing a spider could bring me very bad luck, so to keep the bad luck away, I turned myself around three times while crossing my

20
00:02:07.069 --> 00:02:12.833
chest. But I still felt afraid, and I trembled even

21
00:02:12.834 --> 00:02:16.937
harder. I sat there a long time until I calmed

22
00:02:16.938 --> 00:02:24.141
down. Finally, I heard the clock in the town of St. Petersburg strike 12

23
00:02:24.142 --> 00:02:34.472
times. It was midnight. A twig snapped out in the darkness, and then I heard a little "Me-yow, me-yow," down in the

24
00:02:34.473 --> 00:02:44.133
yard. "Me-yow," I called back softly. Then I climbed out the window, onto the shed, and down to the

25
00:02:44.134 --> 00:02:48.698
ground. And sure enough, there was Tom waiting for

26
00:02:48.699 --> 00:02:52.396
me. Tom and I tiptoed through the widow’s

27
00:02:52.397 --> 00:02:56.269
garden. As we passed the kitchen, I tripped over a

28
00:02:56.270 --> 00:03:02.850
root. Jim, Miss Watson’s black slave, was sitting by the kitchen door when he heard the

29
00:03:02.851 --> 00:03:05.540
noise. "Who’s that?" he called

30
00:03:05.541 --> 00:03:11.002
out. Then he came out into the garden and stood right between

31
00:03:11.003 --> 00:03:16.620
us. Tom and I stood completely still. Jim couldn’t see us in the dark.

32
00:03:16.621 --> 00:03:25.775
"I know I heard something," Jim said. "I’m going to sit down here and listen until I hear that sound again."

33
00:03:25.776 --> 00:03:31.792
Well, first my ankle and my ear started to itch, and then my nose.

34
00:03:31.793 --> 00:03:39.695
I felt as if I’d die if I couldn’t scratch, but if I did, Jim would know we were there.

35
00:03:39.696 --> 00:03:47.050
Just when I couldn’t stand it any more, we heard Jim snoring. He had fallen asleep!

36
00:03:47.051 --> 00:03:51.169
Before we left, Tom played a trick on Jim.

37
00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:56.495
He crept over to Jim, took off his hat, and hung it on a branch.

38
00:03:56.496 --> 00:04:03.849
Tom said that Jim would think witches had moved his hat.

39
00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:11.742
Tom and I went into town where Ben Rogers, Joe Harper, and two or three other boys were waiting for us.

40
00:04:11.743 --> 00:04:18.197
We rowed a boat about four kilometers down the Mississippi River, and came ashore.

41
00:04:18.198 --> 00:04:25.931
There Tom led us to his secret cave, which had an entrance hidden by bushes.

42
00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:33.434
We lit our candles and crawled through a long passageway on our hands and knees.

43
00:04:33.435 --> 00:04:37.681
When we reached the cave, it was damp and cold.

44
00:04:37.682 --> 00:04:43.169
"We’ll start a band of robbers called Tom Sawyer’s Gang," Tom said.

45
00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:48.475
"Everyone who wants to join must take an oath and write his name in blood."

46
00:04:48.476 --> 00:04:54.783
Everyone agreed. Tom got out a piece of paper and wrote down the oath.

47
00:04:54.784 --> 00:05:03.935
It said that we had to promise to be loyal to the band and never tell its secrets. Anyone who told would be killed.

48
00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:12.807
We all said it was a very good oath, and Tom said that he got the words for it from books about pirates and robbers.

49
00:05:12.808 --> 00:05:21.921
Then Ben said that he thought the families of the boys who told secrets should be killed too. So Tom added that to the oath.

50
00:05:21.922 --> 00:05:25.413
Joe pointed out that I didn’t have a family.

51
00:05:25.414 --> 00:05:32.099
Tom replied that I had a father, but the others objected that he’d disappeared a long time ago.

52
00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:39.618
Finally, I said I was willing to give them Miss Watson to kill.

53
00:05:39.619 --> 00:05:47.528
Everyone agreed to that. Then we all stuck our fingers with a pin, and made a mark on the paper with our blood.

54
00:05:47.529 --> 00:05:52.014
"Now," said Ben, "What is our gang going to do?"

55
00:05:52.015 --> 00:05:57.605
"We’re going to wear masks and stop carriages on the road," Tom explained.

56
00:05:57.606 --> 00:06:02.499
"We’ll kill the people and take their watches and money."

57
00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:12.157
It was getting very late, so we decided to meet again next week to decide which folks we would rob and kill. Then we all went home.

58
00:06:12.158 --> 00:06:17.468
By the time I climbed in my window at the widow’s house it was almost dawn.

59
00:06:17.469 --> 00:06:24.708
My new clothes were covered with dirt and I was very tired.

